oglia","gene_id":"ENSG00000102158","module":"brown","kme":0.165923,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.586688,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false},"mathys2019":{"dataset_label":"Mathys et al. 2019","gene_ids":["ENSG00000102158"],"dataset_symbols":["MAGT1"],"explorer":"explorer.html?dataset=mathys2019#gene/MAGT1","cell_types":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_symbol":"MAGT1","gene_symbol_current":"MAGT1","gene_id":"ENSG00000102158","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.985617,"donor_log2fc":-0.150973,"donor_lfcse":0.166561,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-2.18116e-05},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"MAGT1","gene_symbol_current":"MAGT1","gene_id":"ENSG00000102158","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.956584,"donor_log2fc":0.0437883,"donor_lfcse":0.130646,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00238624}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000102158","module":"greenyellow","kme":0.100712,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.56571,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000102158","entrez_id":["84061"],"uniprot":["Q9H0U3"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a ubiquitously expressed magnesium cation transporter protein that localizes to the cell membrane. This protein also associates with N-oligosaccharyl transferase and therefore may have a role in N-glycosylation. Mutations in this gene cause a form of X-linked intellectual disability (XLID). This gene may have multiple in-frame translation initiation sites, one of which would encode a shorter protein with an N-terminus containing a signal peptide at amino acids 1-29. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2017].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9H0U3","text":"Accessory component of the STT3B-containing form of the N-oligosaccharyl transferase (OST) complex which catalyzes the transfer of a high mannose oligosaccharide from a lipid-linked oligosaccharide donor to an asparagine residue within an Asn-X-Ser/Thr consensus motif in nascent polypeptide chains (PubMed:31831667). Involved in N-glycosylation of STT3B-dependent substrates (PubMed:31831667). Specifically required for the glycosylation of a subset of acceptor sites that are near cysteine residues; in this function seems to act redundantly with TUSC3. In its oxidized form proposed to form transient mixed disulfides with a glycoprotein substrate to facilitate access of STT3B to the unmodified acceptor site. Also has oxidoreductase-independent functions in the STT3B-containing OST complex possibly involving substrate recognition. Could indirectly play a role in Mg(2+) transport in epithelial cells (Probable)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}